infographic compare-binary-horizontal-underline-text-vs
data
  title Why REST dodges N+1 and GraphQL walks into it
  desc Same posts-with-authors query — one global JOIN versus isolated per-field resolvers
  compares
    - label REST controller
      children
        - label Hand-written per endpoint
          desc Developer owns the whole response shape in one place
        - label Writes the JOIN up front
          desc SELECT posts JOIN users ON users.id = posts.author_id
        - label One global query plan
          desc The SQL lives in one spot you can read and optimize
        - label 1 DB round-trip
          desc 50 posts and their authors come back in one query
    - label GraphQL resolvers
      children
        - label Isolated per Type.field
          desc A resolver never sees its siblings or how the parent fetched
        - label No place to write the JOIN
          desc Post.author gets one post at a time, args only
        - label No global query plan
          desc Composable by design — the same trait that causes the storm
        - label 1 + N DB round-trips
          desc 51 for 50 posts: 1 list query + 50 author queries
theme
  palette #14b8a6 #f43f5e
